"""Pairwise mean critic for MinAtar (Anakin, single file).  2026-10-31.

D(x, y) approximates Q(x) - Q(y) for state-action pairs x = (s, a), y = (s', a').
Network (PairNet):
  phi(s)   = MinAtarTorso(s)                                  (Conv16 3x3 VALID -> Dense128)
  e(s, a)  = Dense128(relu(Dense128([phi(s), emb(a)])))      (emb: 16-d action embedding)
  g(ex,ey) = Dense1(relu(Dense128([ex, ey])))
  head=free : D(x, y) = g(e_x, e_y)                           (R-C51 style, no constraint)
  head=anti : D(x, y) = g(e_x, e_y) - g(e_y, e_x)            (antisymmetric, D(x, x) = 0)
Action read-out (actor, target greedy action, evaluation): Borda score(s, a) = mean_{b != a} D((s,a), (s,b)).
Pairing (system.n_partners = K, default 1): each transition is x in K pairs with K distinct cyclic shifts.
head=lowrank (2026-10-31): D = f(x)-f(y)+z(x).z'(y)-z(y).z'(x), f=w^T h, z=Z1 h, z'=Z2 h (rank system.pair_rank);
  Borda read-out in closed form; with system.all_pairs=True all m(m-1) ordered pairs of the batch are used, computed as
  m x m matrices (one matmul each).  See 02_方法/交叉加权成对critic_算法描述_20261031.
head=free/anti with system.all_pairs=True (2026-11-01): all m(m-1) ordered pairs with the SAME MLP head, computed by the
  additive decomposition Dense([ex,ey]) = ex K1 + ey K2 + b (Bahdanau-style): U, V once per transition, then
  relu(U_i + V_j) . w2 + b2 for every pair (no per-pair matmul); Borda read-out uses the same decomposition.
head=rc51 (2026-10-31): Relative C51 (R-C51) reproduced from its appendix C on the MinAtar body: (s,a) encoder
  [phi(s), 48-d action embedding] -> 2 x Dense512; pair head [e_x, e_y] -> 2 x Dense512 -> rc_atoms logits over
  [-rc_vmax, rc_vmax]; continuation head (BCE, cont_coef); Bellman uniformization with gbar = gamma, four-way stay/go
  mixture of projected targets; one partner per transition (cyclic shift); greedy actions by Borda score of the mean.
head=sadqn: same-capacity DQN control, Q(s,a) = Dense1(relu(Dense256(e(s,a)))), standard DQN loss on the same
encoder (pair head and continuation head not created).
head=duel_mlp (CW-Duel with an MLP state-pair head, 2026-11-02): D((s,a),(t,b)) = Wg(s,t) + A(s,a) - A(t,b),
  Wg(s,t) = g(phi(s), phi(t)) - g(phi(t), phi(s)), g = Dense1(relu(Dense128([phi_s, phi_t]))) (antisymmetric MLP);
  A = centred advantage stream on phi(s).  Pairing: system.n_partners distinct cyclic shifts (not all pairs).
  Current-state parts of Amax/Bmin ALWAYS from the target network (the online-sg variant diverged on seaquest).
head=duel (CW-Duel, 2026-11-02): D((s,a),(t,b)) = W(s,t) + A(s,a) - A(t,b) on the STATE features phi only
  (no (s,a) encoder).  A(s,.) = adv(phi(s)) - mean_c adv(phi(s))_c (centred advantage, Dueling stream);
  W(s,t) = w(s) - w(t) + z1(s).z2(t) - z2(s).z1(t) (antisymmetric low-rank state-pair head, rank pair_rank;
  pair_rank=0 -> W = w(s) - w(t), the consistent class Q = w + A).  Same-state differences are A(s,a) - A(s,b),
  Borda(s,a) = A/(A-1) A(s,a), greedy = argmax A.  Loss: all m(m-1) ordered pairs, cross weighting; the
  CURRENT-state parts of Amax / Bmin use the online network under stop-gradient (so that for pair_rank=0
  xi_ij = v_j u_i - v_i u_j exactly, u = DQN TD error), next-state parts and a* = argmax A^-(s') the target network.
  See 02_方法/CW-Duel_*_20261102.
head=duel_sa (2026-11-04, CW-Duel with a pairwise (s,a) advantage head): identical to head=duel (same W, same loss,
  all pairs, rho weights, cur_target) except the advantage: psi(s,a) = (s,a) encoder e(s,a) of the free/anti heads
  (Dense128(relu(Dense128([phi(s), emb(a)]))), 16-d action embedding), psi_c(s,a) = psi(s,a) - mean_b psi(s,b)
  (centring in embedding space, every action passed through the encoder once), A(s,a) = w . psi_c(s,a) with a
  LINEAR read-out w (no bias).  Hence A(s,a) - A(t,b) = w . (psi_c(s,a) - psi_c(t,b)), rows of A sum to 0, and the
  same-state pairwise matrix delta_ab = w . (psi(s,a) - psi(s,b)) has row mean A(s,a) (= Borda).  A non-linear
  read-out of the difference would not decompose and would reintroduce the free-head non-identifiability.
head=qcw (2026-11-04, 'RDQN without c, cross-weighted'): D((s,a),(t,b)) = Q(s,a) - Q(t,b) with a plain DQN head
  Q(s,.) = Dense_A(phi(s)) (du_adv, NOT centred; w = 0, no state-pair term).  Loss/pairs/targets = head=duel path.
  Zero set of the cross-weighted residual: u = kappa (1 - g(1-d)) -> Q = Q* - kappa (level only, policy-invariant),
  unlike the centred RDQN loss without c (u = kappa -> Q*_{r-kappa}).
Old single-partner description: a batch of m replay transitions; transition i is paired with transition (i + k) mod m, k ~ U{1..m-1}
(one random shift per update; every pair has two different transitions; each transition is once x and once y).

Bootstrap terms (target network D-, greedy actions a*_x, a*_y at s'_x, s'_y by the target Borda score):
  M     = D-((s'_x,a*_x), (s'_y,a*_y))      Amax = D-((s'_x,a*_x), y)
  Bmin  = D-(x, (s'_y,a*_y))                Dst  = D-(x, y)
Realised Gamma = g(1-d), v = 1 - Gamma.

term=cross (head-free cross weighting, our method).  With k = (1-g)/g:
  xi = v_y r_x - v_x r_y + W1 M + W2 Amax + W3 Bmin + W4 D(x,y)
  W1 = k Gx Gy,  W2 = Gx (v_y - k Gy),  W3 = Gy (v_x - k Gx),  W4 = -v_y - Gy (v_x - k Gx)
  xi is linear in the realised outcomes of two independent transitions, so E[xi | x, y] =
  vbar_x vbar_y (z(x) - z(y)) with z = e/vbar: its zero set (consistent D) is exactly Q(x) - Q(y), no continuation
  head.  Pair types (realised): both continue -> xi = (1-g)[r_x - r_y + g M - D];  x ends, y continues ->
  xi = (1-g) r_x - r_y + g Bmin - D;  both end -> xi = r_x - r_y - D.  Semi-gradient step D += lr * xi/(1-g).
term=unif (R-C51 Bellman uniformization, mean version, Rao-Blackwellised over stay/go, gbar = g):
  continuation head p(x) = sigmoid(Dense1(e_x)), BCE on d with coefficient cont_coef (0.33);
  rho = (1-g)/vhat, vhat = 1 - g(1 - p-(x)) (target-network head), go prob gg = rho (1-d)
  target = rho_x r_x - rho_y r_y + g[gg_x gg_y M + gg_x(1-gg_y) Amax + (1-gg_x) gg_y Bmin + (1-gg_x)(1-gg_y) Dst]
  delta = target - D(x,y)
Loss 0.5 * mean((sg[D + delta] - D)^2)  (semi-gradient; delta = xi/(1-g) for cross).  Adam + global clip,
hard target sync every target_period updates.  Same MinAtar protocol as ff_rdqn (minatar_base).

Same-trajectory pairs (system.same_traj=True, 2026-11-03; head free/anti, term=cross, plain replay): the batch is
built by same_traj.same_traj_batch (m/G uniform anchors + G-1 partners each, drawn uniformly from the other stored items
of the anchor's trajectory, G = system.st_group) and the pairs are all ordered pairs of distinct slots inside a group
(G-1 partners per item instead of n_partners cyclic shifts), loss = 0.5 * weighted mean over those pairs (same
cross-weighted residual).

AL / PAL (system.al_mode = al | pal, system.al_alpha, 2026-11-03; alpal.py): per-transition penalty P from the
target Borda read-out (x (A-1)/A, Q units), cross-weighted residual xi' = xi - alpha (v_y P(x) - v_x P(y)).

rho-kernel (system.pair_rho, same_traj=True, st_cross=0; 2026-11-03): within-group pairs weighted (1-rho) and
rho_kc cross-group partners per slot weighted rho (same_traj.rho_pairs); no extra items.  head=duel (all pairs,
2026-11-04): the same split as an [m, m] weight matrix over ALL cross-group pairs (same_traj.rho_weight_matrix).

Counterfactual same-state pairs (2026-11-02; system.crn=True, head free/anti, term=cross, K partners, not all_pairs):
  every env step also executes b ~ U(A minus {a}) from the same pre-step state (make_step_fn of ff_rdqn;
  system.cf_coupling = crn: shared random numbers, ind: independent rng keys); the buffer item holds both branches.
  Nodes: m real transitions (s_i, a_i, r_i, d_i, s'_i) and m counterfactual ones (s_i, b_i, r^b_i, d^b_i, s'^b_i).
  Loss = 0.5 mean_{8m cross-state pairs among the REAL nodes}(delta^2-form)          (unchanged CW-Pair loss)
       + same_coef * 0.5 mean_{2m same-state pairs (real_i, cf_i), (cf_i, real_i)}(...)
  with the same cross-weighted xi (unbiased under ind; under crn the termination of one branch can correlate with
  the TD error of the other -> known tabular bias, 10-30 design note).  The counterfactual nodes are never paired
  across states.  Greedy actions at s'^b by the same target Borda read-out.  env_calls = 2 x real steps.
"""
